* Buildable ("discrete") version of the 8-transistor cell: real op-amp input amplifier and a
* real two-terminal bias generator. Core identical to BLACKMER8 (Hebert AES 4055 Fig. 4).
*
* Pins: in out ecp ecn sym vcc vee
* Needs subcircuits QNCORE/QPCORE (device library) and OA_IN (op-amp wrapper: inp inn vcc vee out).
*
* Input amplifier: op-amp -> RDRV -> `top`. RDRV makes the drive behave like a transconductance
*   (loop gain no longer scales with the signal-dependent core gm; Hebert section 2.3) and CC,
*   from the op-amp output to its inverting input, closes the loop at high frequency.
* Bias generator: floating shunt regulator between `top` and `bot`.
*   V(top,bot) = Veb(D1) + Veb(D2) + Vbe(D3) + Vbe(QS)  -> 2 PNP + 2 NPN junctions, all near 20 uA,
*   matching the 2 NPN + 2 PNP junctions around the core loop, so the core idles at about the
*   string current and tracks temperature. QS/QP (Sziklai pair) shunt the excess of RSINK's current.
*   RSINK sets the standing current (must exceed the peak signal current Iin+Iout).
.subckt BLACKMER8D in out ecp ecn sym vcc vee RC=1.75 RDRV=1k CC=22p RSINK=6.8k RSTR=27k RPB=30k
+ AR2=1 AR4=1 AR6=1 AR8=1
XOA 0 in vcc vee oa OA_IN
CC1 oa in {CC}
RDRV oa top {RDRV}
* core
XQ1 in  ecn e1 QNCORE
XQ2 out sym e2 QNCORE AR={AR2}
XQ3 in  ecp e3 QPCORE
XQ4 out ecn e4 QPCORE AR={AR4}
XQ5 c5 c6 e1 QPCORE
XQ6 c6 c5 e2 QPCORE AR={AR6}
RC1 c5 bot {RC}
RC2 c6 bot {RC}
XQ7 c7 c8 e3 QNCORE
XQ8 c8 c7 e4 QNCORE AR={AR8}
RC3 c7 top {RC}
RC4 c8 top {RC}
* bias generator
XD1 d1 d1 top QPCORE
XD2 d2 d2 d1  QPCORE
XD3 d2 d2 x   QNCORE
RSTR x bot {RSTR}
XQS qb x bot QNCORE
RPB top qb {RPB}
XQP bot qb top QPCORE
RSINK bot vee {RSINK}
.ends BLACKMER8D
